// Tataka's Wasteland — Bala Kanda
// Source: Valmiki, Bala Kanda, sargas 24-26 (verify)
//
// Line format:   SPEAKER: words      (speaker = a portrait id; no speaker = narration)
// Tags hand control to the game:
//   # panel <id>      show a painted story panel
//   # walk            play the walk section from the chapter data
//   # battle          play the battle from the chapter data
//   # look <mood>     tint the panel: dusk | dawn

# panel tataka
# look dusk
The emptied country. Nothing grows here, and the wind carries grit.
VISHVAMITRA: Once this was Malada and Karusha, rich and full of people.
VISHVAMITRA: Tataka drove them out. Strong as a thousand elephants, she makes the land a waste.
RAMA: She is a woman, revered one. How can I raise a bow against her?

* [Ask who she was]
    VISHVAMITRA: She was born a yakshini, a nature spirit, and was cursed to become a rakshasi.
    VISHVAMITRA: The curse is hers. The ruin of this land is her doing.
* [Say nothing]
    RAMA: ...
-
VISHVAMITRA: A king's son protects the people. Do not hesitate, Rama.
RAMA: Then I will go.

# walk

LAKSHMANA: The ground shook. She is close. I can smell the dust.
VISHVAMITRA: Before the sun sets, Rama!

# battle

# panel tataka
# look dawn
Tataka falls, and the wasteland can be lived in again.
VISHVAMITRA: Now this country can be lived in again.
RAMA: Then it was right.
Pleased, Vishvamitra prepares to give Rama the divine astras.
-> END
